<description>&lt;p&gt;The Colombian army is facing attacks on its forces, including a bomb that hit a police patrol near a Carabineros school in Cali and a methane blast that killed two workers and left two missing at a coal mine, while separate bus accidents in southwestern Colombia and on a motorway caused multiple deaths and injuries. ELN militants negotiated a hostage release with the government, ending a swap deal, and the ELN and FARC dissidents continue fighting for control, leaving civilians under siege. Environmental activists opposing a Canadian-owned copper project face lawfare and smears, and the government is seeking international support to replace coca crops with oil palm. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiywFBVV95cUxNcDBWZ21pM19kM2IzM256RjFabjlJcm03UmFpUVF1VzFwVTQ5M3AzQkhrbFRiVTJONjZ1aTVyTkdjVG1KZlYycVYzeko4OGpzblpMY3EyeTZXX19oVXJvMlFaR3lOV3E2U3ZDTlJIOHlaRWg5bm0zOU1tSDF4Unc1b1lTb2haZzFpT3VzX1NBNFFGMmFCaXhPSHVHZmNXMEgxMEQydXZJbU9FcE9KdzVFd0JaeGFKOHlfSkpWZmhGcGk1V0N1U1pZS3Zncw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTFBuWkdzdzROT2ZZZkhhYmh3M0tLUlJUUk0wUkp0WjBkUW5Qd25CV3V2aDhQOGxDQVFOOEQxcnB1aW9GY0JyNnVvUEZzemV1ZTdjMmpfZzdlNUdLbnllcFE?oc=5&quot;&gt;ColombiaOne.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxPUElMUmoxLVdnWUdNZzNMQUxtWWlJdHZNX3lkWUdobU5ORm9zbGhxblZodFFFT3c5aFU1d0RxZjlwU2tKbnZneXlxX3ZvS1JxWU1lTVNqVDRDcGZMbGNfSE9LTThobXAxdkJQVG9zaFpTQzlfUzhacjl6ZWNOM3FCSXRwZ3N3WnoyNzh3TDlMTXp5bmJnM3VkOHkwdVJEeDY2V21OSXo4RzAtWm55cmJ2Qg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Latin Times&lt;/a